# web: environment variable names only; the inventory in README.md describes each one.
# Copy to .env for local development and set the values locally. Never commit .env files.
# Delete the lines you do not set: an empty value is invalid, while an unset optional variable uses its default.
# Next.js loads .env files itself.
API_BASE_URL=
INTERNAL_BFF_CREDENTIAL=
# Optional, and deferred until the production domain exists. Leave it unset and the app runs normally:
# robots.txt is served without a Sitemap directive and the sitemaps answer 404. Set it to the bare
# origin - scheme and host, no trailing slash - and they turn on with no other change.
PUBLIC_WEB_ORIGIN=
# Optional, and the only thing it does is name one host in the Content-Security-Policy's img-src directive,
# so a stored listing photograph is allowed to load. Leave it unset and the app runs normally with the policy
# it always had - which means a photograph from storage is blocked by the browser rather than a wildcard being
# opened. Set it to the bare origin of the storage host - scheme and host, no trailing slash - and photographs
# appear with no other change. This is not a Supabase variable: the photograph URLs themselves are composed by
# the API from its own SUPABASE_URL and arrive in the response body, and this deployment holds no Supabase
# value of any kind.
MEDIA_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=
